# =============================================================================
# Handled Marketing Website — Environment Variables
# App: apps/website   |   Implements: R34 (ED §6, §11)
#
# Copy this file to apps/website/.env.local and fill in values.
# ALL variables are OPTIONAL: if the Supabase vars are absent, the /api/leads
# route gracefully no-ops (returns { ok: true, stored: false }) so the recorded
# demo never fails. Set them to actually persist leads.
#
# There are NO NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables — the browser never talks to Supabase.
# =============================================================================

# Supabase (OPTIONAL — lead storage)
# Get both from the Supabase dashboard: Settings > API.
# If either is missing, lead capture succeeds in the UI but stores nothing.
SUPABASE_URL=                   # Supabase project URL — Settings > API (Project URL)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=      # SERVER ONLY — service role key, Settings > API. NEVER expose to the browser; used only in app/api/leads/route.ts

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO NEXT_PUBLIC_* VARIABLES IN MVP (ED §12: "Public env vars — none required").
# The site base URL for canonical/OG/sitemap/robots is the single hardcoded
# source `site.url` in content/site.ts (default https://handled.ai). Change it
# there, not via env, for this MVP.
#
# NOT USED IN MVP (documented so they aren't added by mistake):
#   * No LLM / voice / telephony keys — the website has no AI features (ED §8).
#   * No analytics / tracking keys — no third-party pixels in MVP (ED App.A.5).
#   * No payment keys — CTAs route to the demo form, not checkout (ED §2).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
